==Poisons==
In Everquest Legends, Rogues can imbue their attacks with poisons:

*Each melee attack has a chance to apply the rogue's chosen poison.''<<does that include melee special attacks like slam? spellblade? backstab?>>''
*Poisons apply globally to all melee and but not ranged attacks, not on a per-weapon basis.
*Only one utility poison can be active at a time, but all other combat poisons can be active simultaneously, unless otherwise noted on their respective descriptions.
*Once applied poisons last until class swap or character death.
*Coating a weapon in poison takes 2.5sec.
*Poison Strikes are checked against the target's Poison Resistance, and aren't reflectable.


