=Rogue Specific Mechanics=

==Backstab==

For melee combat and backstab damage calculation, dual wield and proc rates please see: [[Game_Mechanics|Game Mechanics]]

In Everquest Legends rogues receive the Chaotic Stab Alternate Advancement for free at level 1 that allows backstab from any position.

To perform backstab the character must have a piercing weapon equipped on his primary/secondary or on one of the <ANY> slots.<br>
''<what about a spear equipped on the ranged slot?><br>''
''<if he has a piercing weapon equipped on main hand with better ratio and a piercing weapon with higher backstab bonus on the secondary or any slot which one will be used for backstab?><br>''
''<what is the cooldown on backstab?><br>''

==Evade==
'''Evade''' is a special rogue-only mechanic that allows in combat use of the hide skill to reduce their agro by lowering their position on the hate lists of mobs that are agro to them. To perform an evasion, the rogue must turn off auto-attack, then use the hide skill. The easiest way to incorporate this into combat is to make a hotkey that does the following (assuming Hide is set to Ability 1):

 /attack off
 /doability 1
 /attack on

When attempting to evade, you will receive one of the following two messages to indicate success or failure:<BR>
*"You have momentarily ducked away from the main combat." (Success, generally ~65% of the time)<BR>
*"Your attempts at ducking clear of combat fail." (Fail)<BR>

==Level 50+ Rogue Traits==
''Not currently implemented in EQ Legends:''  
*Level 51 - Minimum Backstab Damage (76 and increases each level | 1.5 x level, rounded down)  
*Level 55 - Double Backstab Chance, Sneak Speed starts to increase   
*Level 57 - Bind Wound Cap Increased to 70% health once 201+ skill attained.  
*Level 60 - Chance to Assassinate level 46 and below Humanoids when using Backstab or Thrown, Sneak Speed maxed out

